Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js portfolio project.

## What Was Implemented

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm
- Package added to dependencies in package.json
- package-lock.json updated with the new dependency and its transitive dependencies

### 2. Analytics Component Integration
- Added Analytics component to `src/app/layout.tsx` (the root layout for Next.js App Router)
- Imported `Analytics` from `@vercel/analytics/next` (Next.js-specific variant)
- Placed `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag, after the footer

### 3. Implementation Details
The implementation follows the official Vercel Analytics documentation for Next.js App Router:
- Used the framework-specific import path `@vercel/analytics/next`
- Positioned the Analytics component inside the body element for optimal performance
- Preserved all existing code structure, styles, and functionality

### 4. Files Modified
- `portfolio/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `portfolio/package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `portfolio/src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

### 5. Verification Steps Completed
✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ Linter passed with no warnings or errors  
✅ TypeScript compilation successful
✅ No breaking changes to existing functionality

## Next Steps for User

To enable analytics tracking on Vercel:
1. Deploy this code to your Vercel project
2. Navigate to your project dashboard on Vercel
3. Go to the Analytics tab
4. Click "Enable Web Analytics"
5. After the next deployment, analytics will be active

The Analytics component will automatically start collecting page view data once enabled in the Vercel dashboard.
